## Why This Is Asked

Tests deep understanding of tenant isolation, cryptographic best practices, and production-grade key management in KCNA. Evaluates ability to reason about downtime, audits, and validation strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Envelope encryption with per-tenant CMKs
- KMS integration and key rotation without downtime
- Tenant isolation, access controls, and audit integrity
- Replay protection and leakage detection
- Canary/canary-like validation and end-to-end tests

## Code Example

```javascript
function encryptWithTenant(tenantId, plaintext) {
  const cmk = kms.getCMK(tenantId);
  const dataKey = kms.generateDataKey(cmk);
  const iv = crypto.randomBytes(12);
  const cipher = crypto.createCipheriv('aes-256-gcm', dataKey.plain, iv);
  const ciphertext = Buffer.concat([cipher.update(plaintext, 'utf8'), cipher.final()]);
  const tag = cipher.getAuthTag();
  return { ciphertext, tag, keyId: dataKey.keyId, iv: iv, tenantId };
}
```

